1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,560
You've got half a day to explore.

2
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:06,880
Be smart.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:08,620
Keep a low profile.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,200
Like you were never there.

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,460
You must not change the past.

6
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,400
Wait, what are you doing here?

7
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,500
For real, didn't you go overseas?

8
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,600
Don't attract any attention.

9
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:23,020
Hey, don't just run from us.

10
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,340
I don't understand.

11
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:26,460
He and Lu aren't supposed to be back yet.

12
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:29,920
Where'd he go?

13
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:32,320
Okay, are we crazy?

14
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:33,680
That was him, right?

15
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:36,500
Being extra weird.

16
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:40,960
Yeah, or you think we hallucinated it?

17
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:42,500
Maybe it's the heat.

18
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:45,780
You could've warned me she was walking by!

19
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:47,660
This is too strange.

20
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,400
Here, I'm gonna call him.

21
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:52,200
It's not my fault.

22
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:53,660
Some of the cameras are dead.

23
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,380
I can't see through them.

24
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:57,360
We'll work this out, I'm sure.

25
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:01,600
Oh, crap.

26
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:02,800
Where did Dodo go?

27
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:04,180
I don't see him either.

28
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:29,400
I can't help you now.

29
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,240
They've left the radius of my power.

30
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:53,960
Dodo!

31
00:01:53,960 --> 00:02:02,140
We failed the job.

32
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:14,100
It didn't take too long to realize

33
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:16,960
Something has changed in the back of my mind

34
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,320
Your eyes

35
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,600
There ain't nowhere left to hide behind

36
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,100
Time no longer flew like it was

37
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:25,780
When the flash froze everything before

38
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:27,100
Without you

39
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,620
I don't know if I could take this road

40
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:32,060
And I'm about to lose my mind

41
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:34,360
Every minute that I die back in time

42
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,920
Every single existence rewinds

43
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:39,260
Some physical pain in this eye drive

44
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:40,880
All night

45
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:43,140
All the heartaches and the smiles never faded

46
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:44,540
I know you'll be by my side

47
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:45,720
When we make it

48
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:48,320
Come back from the times

49
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,640
Back in time

50
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:55,040
Die back in time

51
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:59,500
Die back in time

52
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:03,720
Die back in time

53
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,940
Die back in time

54
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:25,560
I'm sorry.

55
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:29,940
We tried the security footage, but it was a wash.

56
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:33,520
Thank you.

57
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:35,220
You didn't have to help.

58
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:37,220
I'm grateful.

59
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:41,220
I wanted to tell you before I used to stop by your shop,

60
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:44,220
when I was in college.

61
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:49,220
The day it happened, I saw your son with someone, but said nothing.

62
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:57,220
If only I'd stopped them or told you he'd be here.

63
00:03:57,220 --> 00:04:00,220
I could have saved you from so much pain.

64
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:04,220
I'm so, so sorry.

65
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:10,220
I tried to put it behind me that when I saw you, I didn't even have the courage to say something.

66
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:12,220
Listen to me.

67
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:13,220
It's fine.

68
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:16,220
If I keep on searching, I know I'll find him.

69
00:04:16,220 --> 00:04:20,220
What you just said shows me that I'm right.

70
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:22,220
You've given me hope.

71
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:24,220
More clues are out there somewhere.

72
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:28,220
So I'll keep looking for a decade or more.

73
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:30,220
I swear I won't stop.

74
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:33,220
One day I will find him.

75
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:34,220
You can do it, Triple Star Warriors!

76
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:35,220
Beat the bad guy!

77
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:39,220
As long as we have hope, we won't be defeated so easily!

78
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:44,220
As long as we have hope, we won't be defeated so easily!

79
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:51,220
I'm sure that Dodo is out there waiting for me, dreaming that his parents will bring him home.

80
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:54,220
Daddy… Mommy…

81
00:04:54,220 --> 00:05:01,220
Now then, enough talk of regrets. I should keep searching for new clues.

82
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:07,220
Excuse me. If you don't mind, I want to help out.

83
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:13,220
Thanks. That'd be great. Sorry, I kind of forgot you were there for a second.

84
00:05:13,220 --> 00:05:16,220
Oh dear, it looks like your presence is unremarkable.

85
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:19,220
Dad, you take that back, damn it!

86
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:24,220
By the way, do you happen to have any photos from around the time of the incident?

87
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:27,220
None the cops found helpful. Let me find them.

88
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:32,220
They aren't much, but there's something. Hold on.

89
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:36,220
Whoa. Are you using the same phone you had then?

90
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:46,220
Yes. Happily. I don't want to lose anything saved on it. In case I'm overlooking a clue.

91
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:50,220
When were these photos taken? Close to that day?

92
00:05:50,220 --> 00:05:53,220
Not quite. I would've snapped these the week before.

93
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:58,220
We closed and had a nice day. Just the two of us.

94
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:02,220
After the store opened, we honestly didn't have time to take many pics.

95
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:06,220
Wait! Back up! What was that?

96
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:09,220
Huh? Not sure what you mean.

97
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:14,220
There! That one! Who took this?

98
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:19,220
Huh. Dodo must have taken this one. He loved taking pictures.

99
00:06:19,220 --> 00:06:24,220
I couldn't bring myself to delete even the blurry ones. He might want them. One day.

100
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:29,220
You know, I think this was from that afternoon.

101
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:31,220
Nobody looks too suspicious.

102
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:40,220
This could be it!

103
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:48,220
You don't stand a chance, villain! The powers of justice will take you down!

104
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:52,220
Excellent! Let me borrow your phone.

105
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:57,220
Here, look. It might be the key.

106
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:16,220
Let's go.

107
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:32,220
Star of justice, bringing hope!

108
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:34,220
Star of courage, conquering fear!

109
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:36,220
Star of wisdom, serving knowledge!

110
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:39,220
Orange black milk tea, ice, light sugar.

111
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:44,220
It'll be done soon. Please be patient.

112
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:57,220
Nice.

113
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:02,220
Any moment now, Dodo will be taken from here.

114
00:08:02,220 --> 00:08:07,220
I wasn't able to see the kidnapper's face, or how they grabbed him. So watch out.

115
00:08:07,220 --> 00:08:10,220
Yeah, it's weird. There's a bunch of people around.

116
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:14,220
Who would nab someone in broad daylight with so many witnesses?

117
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:16,220
You need to be careful.

118
00:08:17,220 --> 00:08:19,220
This is our last chance.

119
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:23,220
Whoever took this child will pay. Let's do this.

120
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:29,220
That's it!

121
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:54,220
Be a dear, and give your sweet old auntie the bar back.

122
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:55,220
Auntie?

123
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:59,220
Hm. Why does this smell so good?

124
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:00,220
Oh my god.

125
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:02,220
Drop it!

126
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:06,220
So that's how it went down.

127
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:08,220
No wonder we couldn't figure it out.

128
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,220
Keep focused.

129
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:18,220
Snap out of it!

130
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:20,220
Sweetie, follow me.

131
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:22,220
See? Your parents are too busy.

132
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:27,220
But I'm always more than happy to play with you. Come. We'll have fun at my house.

133
00:09:29,220 --> 00:09:31,220
Hey, why is their kid leaving with someone?

134
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:34,220
Oh, didn't you hear? That's his aunt.

135
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:36,220
His parents are way too swamped here.

136
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:38,220
I'll have a better time with her, I bet.

137
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:40,220
What's wrong with me?

138
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:41,220
I feel dizzy.

139
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:44,220
I can't control my body.

140
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:48,220
But my vision is blurring.

141
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:51,220
You need to stay with me!

142
00:09:51,220 --> 00:09:53,220
Oh, let's check out the shop.

143
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:55,220
The line isn't too long yet.

144
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,220
Hey, it's you!

145
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:08,220
Huh?

146
00:10:09,220 --> 00:10:11,220
Hey, wait. What are you doing here?

147
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:20,220
Dodo!

148
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:21,220
Dodo!

149
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:23,220
Abby?

150
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:24,220
Dodo!

151
00:10:27,220 --> 00:10:28,220
Sorry.

152
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,220
Sweetheart.

153
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:30,220
I know that we're late.

154
00:10:31,220 --> 00:10:34,220
When Gigi's mom came to pick her up from school,

155
00:10:34,220 --> 00:10:37,220
she said that you and mom forgot about me!

156
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,220
Hey, don't listen to her.

157
00:10:40,220 --> 00:10:42,220
Look, for you. Daddy picked out a special toy.

158
00:10:43,220 --> 00:10:47,220
You got the Star of Justice! Can I open it now?

159
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:51,220
Of course. I was late because I wanted to find you all three warriors.

160
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:55,220
So, son, you forgive your old man, don't you?

161
00:10:56,220 --> 00:10:59,220
What are you saying, liar? We're late because you were haggling!

162
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:02,220
You idiot! We should've just paid full price!

163
00:11:02,220 --> 00:11:05,220
Come on, don't be like that. He can hear you.

164
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:06,220
He…

165
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,220
Finally awake.

166
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:24,220
The trafficker drugged you. You've been out a while.

167
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:28,220
Listen up. You're going to be out of time before long.

168
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:30,220
Where am I?

169
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:35,220
I'm not sure. You were unconscious. I couldn't see anything.

170
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:40,220
How could such a horrible person sleep so soundly?

171
00:11:40,220 --> 00:11:42,220
Don't sit there. Investigate.

172
00:11:42,220 --> 00:11:44,220
Don't sit there. Investigate.

173
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:11,220
The Red Sun Hostel?

174
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:20,220
I'm on it. Just a second.

175
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:26,220
There's not one around here, but I see about thirty other locations throughout the country.

176
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:31,220
This kidnapper already took you from the city and hid you.

177
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:34,220
In that case, how did she travel?

178
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:39,220
She would need her ID for public transportation, which means she probably still has it on her.

179
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:43,220
See if you can find a purse or wallet somewhere.

180
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:07,220
Oh no, no, no, no…

181
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:10,220
Mine's my father and my father.

182
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:11,220
It's grown for that sister!

183
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:13,220
I'm one of her parents, but…

184
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:15,320
And I'm doing the same.

185
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:19,220
And that's what she's treating me anyway…

186
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:22,220
I know what, why are we-

187
00:13:23,220 --> 00:13:24,220
Oh, what…

188
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:26,220
That's it.

189
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:29,220
Oh, that's great.

190
00:13:30,220 --> 00:13:32,220
Yeah, I didn't work for a assistir.

191
00:13:32,220 --> 00:13:58,560
Jackpot!

192
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:04,560
Damn, it's tangled in some talisman.

193
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:08,560
She's the evil one, but she's afraid of ghosts.

194
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:10,560
Makes no sense.

195
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:14,560
Hurry, you don't have much time left.

196
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:40,560
Bingo.

197
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:42,560
Her name's Mei Pien.

198
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:46,560
Her ID number is 594810.

199
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:50,560
81-81-81-81-0.

200
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:58,560
Very close.

201
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:22,560
Whoa, those moves I learned from Master Suen are no joke!

202
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:23,560
I'm awesome!

203
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:25,560
Watch carefully, you two.

204
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:27,560
This is called sending you to heaven.

205
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:28,560
Right?

206
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:29,560
Right.

207
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:32,560
This move can be lethal.

208
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:33,560
Got that?

209
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:35,560
Only use it for emergencies and don't use it on people.

210
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,560
She's lucky I'm a child right now.

211
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:38,560
I could have killed her.

212
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:39,560
You little brat.

213
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:42,560
Most kids are too scared to fight back.

214
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:43,560
They just cry.

215
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:46,560
But you, you dare touch me?

216
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:49,560
I'm gonna cut off your legs.

217
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:52,560
Then I'll rip out your tongue.

218
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:55,560
You'll scream and spend the rest of your life in pain.

219
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:56,560
Huh!

220
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:57,560
Evil me, Pien.

221
00:15:57,560 --> 00:15:58,560
You heartless waste!

222
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:01,560
I can't believe how deranged you are!

223
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:03,560
Even the gods won't tolerate you anymore.

224
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,560
They send me here to teach you a lesson!

225
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:08,560
Maniac kid, what are you talking about?

226
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:18,560
Listen here, old lady.

227
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:20,560
In three years you'll be brought to justice.

228
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:21,560
Take my advice.

229
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,560
Look after this kid.

230
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:27,560
Start doing good deeds so when the end arrives you can beg for mercy!

231
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:35,560
Otherwise after you die you'll spend an eternity burning in the depths of hell!

232
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:37,560
You're possessed.

233
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:39,560
Who are you?

234
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:42,560
I am your ancestor.

235
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:43,560
Father!

236
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:44,560
Father!

237
00:16:44,560 --> 00:16:45,560
Father!

238
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:46,560
Please help me!

239
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:57,560
Our ancestors have sent me a warning!

240
00:16:57,560 --> 00:17:00,560
Ancestry's have sent me a warning!

241
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,760
Liang, try to relax.

242
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:16,360
If you're nervous, your kid's sure to pick up on something like that.

243
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:18,360
I'm not nervous, just excited.

244
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:20,560
I've waited so long for this moment.

245
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:23,960
I'm still trying to figure out how you got the info on this human trafficker lady.

246
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,960
Don't leave me guessing, man. What's the secret?

247
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:31,560
I met lots of helpful people. I have them to thank.

248
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:34,560
This world still has good humans in it.

249
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:38,560
Honey, Dodo is finally returning.

250
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:43,560
You need to prepare yourself in case the Ax Shire doesn't recognize you after three years.

251
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:46,560
It's important that you take your time and try not to rush him.

252
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:50,560
Yes, I understand that. And I'm ready. We'll work through this.

253
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:55,560
Hey, there's the van!

254
00:17:57,560 --> 00:18:03,560
Let us know that we have to hug you after two months later.

255
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:05,560
Well, it does, earlier.

256
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:08,560
Yes!

257
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,560
Doodo!

258
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:16,560
My son!

259
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:17,560
We're here! businessman!

260
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:19,560
You're here! You're safe!

261
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:23,560
Do you remember your daddy, Bodo?

262
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:27,560
I'm sorry. It took so long.

263
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:38,560
Wow! It's the heroes! Hi there!

264
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:43,560
Star of Courage! Conquering fear!

265
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:45,560
Star of Wisdom! Serving knowledge!

266
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:48,560
Star of Justice! Bringing hope!

267
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:51,560
We are the Triple Star Warriors!

268
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:54,560
I'm so sorry, Dodo.

269
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:56,560
I was trying to find these warriors for you.

270
00:18:56,560 --> 00:18:58,560
That's why I was late.

271
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:02,560
Now, kid, do you think you can forgive your old man?

272
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:05,560
Daddy! Daddy!

273
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:10,560
Son! You're home!

274
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:14,560
Awesome! We did it!

275
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:16,560
Our job is done!

276
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:21,560
Dodo, it's you! Welcome back!

277
00:19:21,560 --> 00:19:23,560
Our family is finally home again!

278
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:46,560
Please, sir. I swear to you, I haven't harmed a single person in the last three years. And him. I raised that boy as though he were my own flesh and blood. He got the best care I could afford. I've repented my past mistakes every day. I beg you.

279
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:52,560
Hey, Mei Pien! Stay on the right track! Your ancestors are watching!

280
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:55,560
I hear you, Spirit! Thank you!

281
00:19:55,560 --> 00:20:02,560
Cut it out! Pretending to be crazy isn't going to result in a lighter sentence or a judge's mercy.

282
00:20:02,560 --> 00:20:04,560
Chun Bin, take her inside and start interrogating.

283
00:20:04,560 --> 00:20:06,560
My ancestors are speaking to me again!

284
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:24,560
So, your name is Chung Shaoshu, is that right? And the white-haired boy is Lu Guang. Which means, the girl is Chaoling. All the rumors online about a powerful old witch are just a cover story. You're the ones who have the ability to enter photographs, aren't you?

285
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:37,560
I have no idea what you're talking about. Then explain this to me. Are you kidding? Chun was just here a few days ago looking at this. Why are you bugging me about a cold case?

286
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:49,560
Stop there! What is it? This guy a suspect or something?

287
00:20:49,560 --> 00:21:06,560
What I'm wondering is simple. Why do you show up in surveillance footage from the milk tea shop three years ago? Hey, relax. I'm just curious about how your power works. Take this envelope. It contains photos from a major case I've got.

288
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:16,560
I could use your help, if you don't mind. Hold on. You should ask me. I decide if we help.

289
00:21:36,560 --> 00:22:04,240
If I can wait for my heart, the

290
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:34,220
Oh, oh, oh, oh.

